# A negative control passes only if the sabotaged run printed a `not ok ` line AND no `Bail out!` line
# (a hung observed call prints `Bail out!` and exits 70; the old `findstr "not ok "` alone passed that
# if an earlier test had failed as intended).  The pipe hides the exit status, so this reads the TAP:
# capture stdout to a file, then the `not ok ` check, then `Bail out!` must be absent.
